@startuml
title Figure 68 — Timing diagram: data input/output in dual data rate mode

clock "CLK" as clk with period 1

concise "Input" as input
concise "Output" as output

@0
input is DATA
output is I

@0.25
input is DATA

@0.5
input is DATA

@0.75
input is DATA

@1
input is DATA

@1.25
input is DATA

@1.5
input is DATA

@1.75
input is Invalid

@0.1
output is DATA

@0.6
output is DATA

@1.1
output is DATA

note top of clk
  tPP (clock period)
end note

note bottom of input
  tISUddr = Input setup time (DDR)
  tIHddr = Input hold time (DDR)
  Data sampled on both edges of clock
  (not applicable for CMD line)
end note

note bottom of output
  tODLYddr(min) = Output delay minimum (DDR)
  tODLYddr(max) = Output delay maximum (DDR)
end note

note right of clk
  min (VIH)
  max (VIL)
end note

note right of input
  min (VIH)
  max (VIL)
end note

note right of output
  min (VOH)
  max (VOL)
end note
@enduml